---
description: Commit message format with fix/feat/refactor(R5) prefix
alwaysApply: true
---

Commit message rules:

- Every commit subject must start with exactly one of: `fix(R5)`, `feat(R5)`, `refactor(R5)`.
- After the prefix, add one space, then a single-line description of what changed (no second subject line, no body required unless the user asks for detail).
- Use present tense or imperative: "add", "fix", "remove", not "added" or "adding".
- The description should be specific enough to understand the commit without opening the diff.

Prefix meaning:

- `fix(R5)` — bug fix, regression fix, broken tests, incorrect behavior.
- `feat(R5)` — new behavior, new module, new action, new test coverage for new capability.
- `refactor(R5)` — structure or naming change without intended behavior change; docs-only vault edits; dependency or tooling cleanup.

Examples:

```
feat(R5) filter conv residual actions with ShapeProp output shape equality
fix(R5) skip ResNet layer3 to layer4 pairs that mismatch spatial size on add
refactor(R5) rewrite FX Shape Probe vault page with per-function sections
feat(R5) add call_module_output_shapes and wire it in AddResConvLayer
```